  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14197487/assets/d9a2a079f471072c80becb1188a2862f6f5d0d699eb40989b01c27a1f079fc42.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-10,6].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $13.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-10,6]$ given that $f(-10)=-2.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
